Commit 22e0e2b6, parked on phase/8.4 (tag deleted 2026-10-16)
Subject: fix(web-ui): print a CLI login example that works, and name KGX's graph access requirement

Card 30. `s3 login` with no argument fails as printed: main.py's parser
requires an email positional. CLI_EXAMPLE now sets S3_BASE_URL to this
deployment and calls `s3 login you@example.org`, so pasting the example
targets the right server instead of the CLI's localhost default. The KGX
command is kept as printed, since it is otherwise correct, and the card's
body now says plainly that it needs operator-granted read-only graph
database credentials, so a public reader is told why it will not run for
them instead of being led to a command that fails silently.


